    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nRelevant: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/32280\nAnd see this discussion: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/40640\n\nI'd like to control the sort of files rendered by `dir.lua`. My needs are very specific, but:\n\n- Sort by file modification timestamp\n- Sort ascending and descending\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThere are various knobs to control the sorting!",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The approach in vim-dirvish, which I think was very successful (conceptually/intuitively), is to simply allow, and encourage, modifications to the dir buffer. Just need to provide well-defined hooks. Then users (and maybe some builtin defaults) can easily sort the contents in arbitrary ways.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-08T18:12:52Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40641#issuecomment-4917842111",
